# Sovren Project Rules

## Core Documentation References

All team members and AI contributors must read, understand, and follow these core documents:

1. **CODE_OF_CRAFT.md** - The 11 Commandments of Elite Engineering Excellence
2. **docs/quality-gates.md** - Quality gates that all code changes must pass
3. **docs/development/mermaid-requirement.md** - Mandatory Mermaid diagram requirements
4. **docs/development/mermaid-diagram-guide.md** - Guide for creating effective Mermaid diagrams
5. **docs/development/user-story-implementation.md** - User story implementation workflow
6. **CHANGELOG.md** - History of all changes and implementations

## Mandatory Requirements

### Visual Architecture Documentation

- **ALL** user story implementations MUST include the required Mermaid diagrams
- Diagrams MUST follow the standards defined in the Mermaid diagram guide
- Pull requests without the required diagrams WILL be rejected
- No exceptions to the diagram requirements are permitted

### Mermaid Diagram Linking Requirements (MANDATORY)

**CRITICAL RULE**: All Mermaid diagrams MUST be properly linked with visual rendering capabilities:

1. **Create Diagram Files**: Save all Mermaid diagrams as `.mmd` files in `/docs/architecture/diagrams/`
2. **Visual GitHub Links**: ALWAYS include GitHub-rendered diagram links using this format:
   ```markdown
   ![Diagram Name](https://github.com/owner/repo/blob/main/docs/architecture/diagrams/diagram-name.mmd)
   ```
3. **Multiple Link Formats**: Provide multiple viewing options:

   ```markdown
   ## 📊 Architecture Diagrams

   ### System Architecture

   - **[📊 View on GitHub](https://github.com/owner/repo/blob/main/docs/architecture/diagrams/system-architecture.mmd)** - Auto-rendered visual
   - **[🔗 Interactive Editor](https://mermaid.live/edit#your-encoded-diagram)** - Edit and customize
   - **[📁 Source File](docs/architecture/diagrams/system-architecture.mmd)** - Raw Mermaid code
   ```

4. **Documentation Integration**: Every documentation file that references architecture MUST include visual diagram links
5. **Validation Reports**: All validation reports MUST include working visual diagram links, not just embedded code
6. **README Updates**: Update relevant README files with proper diagram links

**ENFORCEMENT**: Any documentation or validation report without proper visual diagram links will be REJECTED. No exceptions.

### Quality Gates

- All code changes MUST pass the quality gates defined in docs/quality-gates.md
- Test coverage MUST meet or exceed 95% for all new code
- Documentation MUST be complete and up-to-date
- Technical debt MUST be actively managed and minimized

### Deployment Integration (MANDATORY - Effective 2025-10-27)

**Following Epic 006 completion, ALL story implementations MUST integrate with automated CI/CD pipelines:**

- **CI/CD Integration**: All code changes MUST trigger and pass automated quality gates
- **Staging Deployment**: All merged PRs MUST successfully deploy to staging environment
- **Health Checks**: All services MUST implement `/health`, `/ready`, and `/live` endpoints
- **Smoke Tests**: All deployments MUST pass automated smoke tests (28+ tests)
- **Production Ready**: Stories are NOT complete until staging deployment succeeds
- **Rollback Tested**: All deployments MUST support automatic rollback (< 2 minutes)

**Reference**: [docs/development/DEPLOYMENT_INTEGRATION_STANDARDS.md](docs/development/DEPLOYMENT_INTEGRATION_STANDARDS.md)

**Agent Requirements**:
- Create PR with deployment checklist
- Verify CI/CD checks passing
- Confirm staging auto-deployment success
- Validate health checks passing
- Document deployment status in completion summary
- Include deployment verification commands in output

### Code of Craft

- All code MUST adhere to the 11 Commandments in CODE_OF_CRAFT.md
- Code reviews MUST enforce these commandments without exception
- New team members MUST read and acknowledge these commandments before contributing

## Implementation Process

1. Read and understand the user story requirements
2. Create the required Mermaid diagrams BEFORE implementation
3. Implement the code following TDD principles
4. Ensure all quality gates pass
5. Update documentation and CHANGELOG.md
6. Submit pull request with all required artifacts
7. **Verify CI/CD pipeline execution and pass all checks** ✅
8. **Confirm staging deployment successful** ✅
9. **Validate health checks and smoke tests passing** ✅
10. **Document deployment status in completion summary** ✅

## Enforcement

These rules are enforced through:

1. Automated checks in the CI/CD pipeline
2. Pull request templates with mandatory checklist items
3. Code review process that verifies compliance
4. Quality gates that block non-compliant changes

No exceptions to these rules are permitted without explicit approval from the engineering leadership team.
